{"id":"h6-02-p2","title":"Design a rate limiter","scopeHtml":"<p>Scope: token bucket, sliding window, Redis Lua atomicity, distributed limiting, API and headers, failure modes. Questions are still to be written.</p>","notes":[{"id":"requirements","title":"Requirements","html":"<p><strong>A rate limiter caps how many requests a client may make in a time window, and rejects the extra ones.</strong> It protects services from abuse, bugs (a client retry loop) and overload, and enforces plans (\"free tier: 100 requests/min\"). Stripe, GitHub, Twitter and Cloudflare all publish limits.</p>\n<p><strong>Functional</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Limit by key: user ID, API key, IP, or endpoint (for example <code>POST /login</code> stricter than <code>GET /feed</code>).</li>\n<li>Return a clear rejection and tell the client when to retry.</li>\n<li>Rules configurable without a deploy.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Non-functional</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Adds under 2 ms to each request (it is in the hot path).</li>\n<li>Works across many app servers (a distributed counter, not per-server).</li>\n<li>Highly available: if the limiter breaks, the product should not go down (decide fail-open vs fail-closed).</li>\n<li>Reasonably accurate; small over-allowance is acceptable.</li>\n</ul>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 613.2 130\" width=\"613.2\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Where it sits\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 65 L158 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 65 L158 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M261.2 65 L317.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M261.2 65 L317.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M427.6 34 L483.6 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M427.6 34 L483.6 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M261.2 65 L317.2 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M261.2 65 L317.2 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"43\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Client</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"43\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"209.6\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">API gateway</text><rect x=\"317.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"372.4\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Rate limiter</text><rect x=\"317.2\" y=\"74\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"372.4\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">App server</text><rect x=\"483.6\" y=\"43\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"542.4\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Counter store</text></svg><figcaption>Where it sits</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> Where to put the limiter: in the gateway (one place, easy, reversible), in each service (flexible, duplicated), or in a client SDK (cannot be trusted). Gateway is the standard choice. Moving it later is cheap, but the choice of algorithm affects client-visible behaviour, so changing it can surprise customers.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A bouncer at a club counting how many people entered in the last minute.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Forgetting to ask: per user, per IP, or per endpoint? hard or soft limit?</li>\n<li>Designing a single-server limiter and ignoring distribution.</li>\n<li>Not deciding fail-open vs fail-closed.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"api","title":"API","html":"<p>The limiter is mostly internal, but the client-facing contract matters.</p>\n<p><strong>Response headers on every call</strong> (de-facto GitHub/Stripe style, IETF draft <code>RateLimit-*</code>):</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>HTTP/1.1 200 OK</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>X-RateLimit-Limit: 100</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>X-RateLimit-Remaining: 37</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>X-RateLimit-Reset: 1731150060        (unix time window resets)</span></span></code></pre>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span>HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Retry-After: 12</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>Content-Type: application/json</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span>{ \"error\": \"rate_limited\", \"retryAfterSeconds\": 12 }</span></span></code></pre>\n<p><strong>Internal check API</strong> (gateway to limiter service, or a library call):</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">POST /internal/check</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">{ </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"key\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"user:42\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"rule\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"api-default\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"cost\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">1</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">200</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> { </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"allowed\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">true</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"remaining\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">37</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"resetMs\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">12000</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> }</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">200</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> { </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"allowed\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">false</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"remaining\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">0</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">, </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">\"retryAfterMs\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">12000</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> }</span></span></code></pre>\n<p><strong>Rules config (hot-reloaded from a config store):</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">rules</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">:</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  - </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">id</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">api-default</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">    key</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">user_id</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">    limit</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">100</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">    window</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">60s</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">    algorithm</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">token_bucket</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">    burst</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">20</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">  - </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">id</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">login</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">    key</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">ip</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">    limit</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">5</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#22863A;--shiki-dark:#85E89D\">    window</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">: </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">60s</span></span></code></pre>\n<p><strong>Industry example.</strong> Stripe returns 429 and recommends exponential backoff; GitHub documents <code>X-RateLimit-*</code> headers and 5,000 requests/hour for authenticated calls.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> The sign on the club door showing \"capacity 100, inside now 63\".</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Returning 403 or 500 instead of 429.</li>\n<li>Omitting <code>Retry-After</code>, so clients retry immediately and make it worse.</li>\n<li>Not including a <code>cost</code> for expensive calls.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"estimates","title":"Estimates","html":"<p>Assume 500M requests/day to the API.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Quantity</th>\n<th>Calculation</th>\n<th>Result</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>Average QPS</td>\n<td>500M / 86,400</td>\n<td>about 5,800/s</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Peak QPS</td>\n<td>3x</td>\n<td>about 17,000/s</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Active keys</td>\n<td>10M users in a minute</td>\n<td>10M</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Memory per key (token bucket)</td>\n<td>key 20 B + tokens 8 B + timestamp 8 B + overhead ~64 B</td>\n<td>~100 B</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Total memory</td>\n<td>10M x 100 B</td>\n<td>~1 GB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Sliding-log memory (100 req/min)</td>\n<td>10M x 100 timestamps x 8 B</td>\n<td>~8 GB (much worse)</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>17,000 checks/s is small for one Redis node (100k+ simple ops/s). Memory is the lever that picks the algorithm: counters and buckets are tiny, per-request logs are not.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 475.6 68\" width=\"475.6\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Check path: one Redis round trip per request\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M290 34 L346 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M290 34 L346 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Gateway</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"224\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Limiter library</text><rect x=\"346\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"404.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Redis cluster</text></svg><figcaption>Check path: one Redis round trip per request</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> Counting people with a clicker (one number) versus writing a name for each person (a long list).</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Picking sliding log without computing memory at scale.</li>\n<li>Ignoring that each check is a network hop (budget 1 ms).</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"high-level-design","title":"High-level design","html":"<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 864.8 130\" width=\"864.8\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Distributed rate limiting with a central store\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M122.4 34 L178.4 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M122.4 34 L178.4 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;0.201;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M296 65 L352 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M296 65 L352 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.200;0.400;0.401;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M455.2 65 L511.2 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M455.2 65 L511.2 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.400;0.600;0.601;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M664.8 65 L720.8 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M664.8 65 L720.8 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;0.801;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M664.8 65 L720.8 96\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M664.8 65 L720.8 96\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.600;0.800;0.801;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M122.4 96 L511.2 65\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M122.4 96 L511.2 65\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"4s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.200;0.201;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"67.2\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Client</text><rect x=\"12\" y=\"74\" width=\"110.4\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"67.2\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Rules config</text><rect x=\"178.4\" y=\"43\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"237.20000000000002\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Load balancer</text><rect x=\"352\" y=\"43\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"403.6\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">API gateway</text><rect x=\"511.2\" y=\"43\" width=\"153.6\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"588\" y=\"69\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Limiter middleware</text><rect x=\"720.8\" y=\"12\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"786.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Redis cluster</text><rect x=\"720.8\" y=\"74\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"786.8\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Backend service</text></svg><figcaption>Distributed rate limiting with a central store</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Flow</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>Request arrives; middleware builds the key (for example <code>rl:user:42:api-default</code>).</li>\n<li>It runs one atomic operation in Redis (Lua script) that refills, checks and decrements.</li>\n<li>Allowed: forward and add headers. Denied: return 429 with <code>Retry-After</code>.</li>\n<li>Rules are cached locally and refreshed from a config service every 30 s.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Why Redis.</strong> In-memory, single-threaded atomic scripts, TTL for auto cleanup, Cluster for sharding by key. Alternatives: Memcached (no scripts, but <code>incr</code> works for fixed window), a local in-process limiter (no shared state, loses accuracy across N servers), or a dedicated service (adds a network hop but centralises logic).</p>\n<p><strong>Decision gravity.</strong> A central store gives accurate global limits but a new dependency in the hot path; local limits are fast and resilient but allow N times the limit. Many companies use both: local approximate limit first, then global. Reversible, since the algorithm sits behind a small interface.</p>\n<p><strong>Industry examples.</strong> Stripe describes a Redis-based token bucket; Cloudflare uses a sliding-window approximation at the edge; Envoy supports a global rate limit service (Lyft's <code>ratelimit</code>) plus a local token bucket.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> One shared clipboard at the club door versus each doorman keeping their own count.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Counting per app server and calling it \"global\".</li>\n<li>Reading then writing in two Redis calls (race condition).</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"deep-dives","title":"Deep dives","html":"<h3>The algorithms</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Fixed window counter.</strong> <code>INCR key</code>, <code>EXPIRE key 60</code>. Cheap, but a burst at a window boundary can allow 2x the limit (100 at 10:00:59 and 100 at 10:01:00).</li>\n<li><strong>Sliding window log.</strong> Store every request timestamp in a sorted set; count those in the last 60 s. Exact, but memory heavy (see estimates).</li>\n<li><strong>Sliding window counter.</strong> Keep the current and previous window counts and weight: <code>prev x (1 - elapsed/window) + current</code>. Tiny memory, error of a few percent (Cloudflare reported about 0.003% wrong decisions in their data).</li>\n<li><strong>Token bucket.</strong> A bucket holds up to <code>burst</code> tokens and refills at a steady rate; each request takes one. Allows bursts and enforces an average. Stripe and AWS API Gateway use it.</li>\n<li><strong>Leaky bucket.</strong> Requests go in a queue that drains at a fixed rate; smooths output but adds latency and drops when full. Good for traffic shaping, e.g. NGINX <code>limit_req</code>.</li>\n</ol>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 582.4 68\" width=\"582.4\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Token bucket: tokens refill over time, each request spends one\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M144 34 L200 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M144 34 L200 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.333;0.334;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M339.2 34 L395.2 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M339.2 34 L395.2 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"2.4000000000000004s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.333;0.667;0.668;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"132\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"78\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Refill (rate r)</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"12\" width=\"139.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"269.6\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Bucket (burst B)</text><rect x=\"395.2\" y=\"12\" width=\"175.20000000000002\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"482.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Request takes 1 token</text></svg><figcaption>Token bucket: tokens refill over time, each request spends one</figcaption></figure>\n<p><strong>Chosen:</strong> token bucket as default (burst-friendly, O(1) memory), sliding window counter where strictness matters (login attempts).</p>\n<p><strong>Worked example.</strong> Limit 100/min, burst 20: refill rate 100/60 = 1.67 tokens/s, bucket cap 20. A client idle for 12 s has 20 tokens and can send 20 at once, then 1.67/s.</p>\n<h3>Atomic check in Redis</h3>\n<p>Two clients checking at once must not both pass. Use one Lua script (Redis runs it atomically, no interleaving):</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6A737D;--shiki-dark:#6A737D\"># KEYS[1]=bucket key; ARGV: rate(tokens/s), capacity, now_ms, cost</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">LUA</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> =</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> \"\"\"</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">local d = redis.call('HMGET', KEYS[1], 'tokens', 'ts')</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">local tokens = tonumber(d[1]) or tonumber(ARGV[2])</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">local ts = tonumber(d[2]) or tonumber(ARGV[3])</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">local delta = math.max(0, tonumber(ARGV[3]) - ts) / 1000</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">tokens = math.min(tonumber(ARGV[2]), tokens + delta * tonumber(ARGV[1]))</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">local allowed = tokens >= tonumber(ARGV[4])</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">if allowed then tokens = tokens - tonumber(ARGV[4]) end</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">redis.call('HSET', KEYS[1], 'tokens', tokens, 'ts', ARGV[3])</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">redis.call('PEXPIRE', KEYS[1], 120000)</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">return allowed and 1 or 0</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">\"\"\"</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Use Redis server time (<code>TIME</code>) or one NTP-synced clock source; mixed client clocks cause drift. PEXPIRE removes idle keys so memory self-cleans.</p>\n<h3>Scaling and sharding</h3>\n<p>Redis Cluster hashes the key to 16,384 slots; each user lives on one shard, so a check is a single-shard call. 17,000/s fits one node, but run 3 primaries with 1 replica each for availability and headroom. A <strong>hot key</strong> (one abusive IP at 100k/s) hammers one shard: add a local pre-filter that blocks it for 1 s after the first deny.</p>\n<figure class=\"flow\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 627.6000000000001 68\" width=\"627.6000000000001\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two-layer limiter: cheap local check first, then global\"><defs><marker id=\"fa\" viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\" refX=\"9\" refY=\"5\" markerWidth=\"7\" markerHeight=\"7\" orient=\"auto\"><path d=\"M0 0L10 5L0 10z\" style=\"fill:var(--muted)\"/></marker></defs><path d=\"M102 34 L158 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M102 34 L158 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.000;0.250;0.251;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M275.6 34 L331.6 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M275.6 34 L331.6 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.250;0.500;0.501;1\"/></circle><path d=\"M456.40000000000003 34 L512.4000000000001 34\" style=\"stroke:var(--muted);fill:none\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" marker-end=\"url(#fa)\"/><circle class=\"flow-dot\" r=\"5\" style=\"fill:var(--accent)\" opacity=\"0\"><animateMotion dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" path=\"M456.40000000000003 34 L512.4000000000001 34\" keyPoints=\"0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;1\" calcMode=\"linear\"/><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" dur=\"3.2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\" values=\"0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.500;0.750;0.751;1\"/></circle><rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"90\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"57\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Request</text><rect x=\"158\" y=\"12\" width=\"117.60000000000001\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"216.8\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Local limiter</text><rect x=\"331.6\" y=\"12\" width=\"124.8\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"394\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Global limiter</text><rect x=\"512.4000000000001\" y=\"12\" width=\"103.2\" height=\"44\" rx=\"22\" style=\"fill:var(--surface);stroke:var(--accent)\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"/><text x=\"564.0000000000001\" y=\"38\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"13\" style=\"fill:var(--ink)\">Redis shard</text></svg><figcaption>Two-layer limiter: cheap local check first, then global</figcaption></figure>\n<h3>Failure modes and decisions</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Redis down:</strong> fail-open (allow) for normal APIs so an outage does not become a total outage; fail-closed for security-sensitive limits (login, OTP). Make this per-rule. Add a short circuit breaker with 50 ms timeout.</li>\n<li><strong>Replica lag after failover:</strong> counters may reset, allowing a short over-allowance; acceptable.</li>\n<li><strong>Race between servers</strong> is solved by the atomic script; do not do GET then SET.</li>\n<li><strong>Thundering herd after window reset:</strong> add jitter to <code>Retry-After</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Multi-tier and fairness</h3>\n<p>Layer limits: per-IP (anonymous), per-user, per-endpoint, global protection (total QPS to the DB). Use weights (<code>cost</code>) for heavy calls (search = 5 tokens). Return <code>Retry-After</code> so well-behaved clients back off.</p>\n<p><strong>Everyday analogy.</strong> A token bucket is a jar of coins that refills slowly; you can spend several at once but cannot spend more than you have.</p>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Not knowing the boundary-burst flaw of fixed windows.</li>\n<li>Choosing sliding log at 10M users.</li>\n<li>Fail-closed everywhere, so a Redis blip takes the whole API down.</li>\n<li>Using client wall clocks for refill timing.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"what-interviewers-look-for","title":"What interviewers look for","html":"<ul>\n<li>Ask what to limit by and what the limit means before designing.</li>\n<li>Compare at least 3 algorithms with memory and accuracy trade-offs, and pick one with a reason.</li>\n<li>Know why atomicity matters and show a Lua script or <code>INCR</code>+<code>EXPIRE</code>.</li>\n<li>Discuss distributed concerns: shared store, sharding, hot keys, clock source.</li>\n<li>State fail-open vs fail-closed and per-rule exceptions.</li>\n<li>Mention client behaviour: 429, <code>Retry-After</code>, headers, backoff with jitter.</li>\n<li>Seniors add local+global layering, config hot reload, observability (allowed/denied rate per rule, p99 limiter latency) and abuse that rotates IPs.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Common interview traps.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Describing only the algorithm and never the distributed system around it.</li>\n</ul>"},{"id":"summary","title":"Summary","html":"<ul>\n<li>A limiter is a counter per key with a rule, checked at the gateway; 429 plus <code>Retry-After</code> on rejection.</li>\n<li>Token bucket is the best default (burst plus steady rate, tiny memory); sliding window counter for strict limits; fixed window has a 2x boundary burst.</li>\n<li>Make the check atomic with a Redis Lua script; shard by key; add a local pre-filter for hot keys.</li>\n<li>About 17k checks/s and ~1 GB for 10M keys: one small Redis cluster is enough.</li>\n<li>Fail-open for general APIs, fail-closed for login/OTP; choose per rule.</li>\n<li>The algorithm is reversible behind an interface, but customers feel behaviour changes, so migrate carefully.</li>\n</ul>"}],"questions":[]}